[{:seon.task/name "ns-keeps-its-metadata"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by lane AGENTS working as a Seon agent (2026-10-21), and earlier by N1: Jolt's (ns ^:scratch foo) does not attach :scratch (or any metadata) to the namespace, so the \"declared ^:scratch\" namespace seon.program describes cannot be declared from the REPL; only seon.agent/make-ns! sets it, through alter-meta! (agent.clj:350), and seon.program/recording reapplies ns metadata as a stopgap (program.clj:125). On the JVM, (meta (find-ns 'foo)) holds the ns form's metadata. Fix in our Jolt fork's ns macro / host/chez/ns.ss (a jolt/<topic> branch): the ns form's metadata (and docstring, attr-map) lands on the namespace; then the stopgap and make-ns!'s alter-meta! go (every definition happens once)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.program-test/a-scratch-ns-declared-at-the-repl-stays-scratch}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-built-binary-requires-a-stdlib-namespace-it-did-not-compile"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by lane TESTS (2026-10-21) importing test/ into a root: in a root booted from target/seon (cd target, ./seon root), `(require 'fipp.engine)` answers `Could not locate clojure/core/rrb_vector.jolt (or .clj/.cljc) on the source roots`, and `(vec (jolt.host/source-roots))` is [\"./src\" \"./resources\" \"./reference-code/persistent-sorted-set/src\" \"jolt-core\" \"stdlib\" \"vendor/fs/src\" ...]: relative paths, resolved against the process's cwd (target/), where none exists. clojure.core.rrb-vector is Jolt's own stdlib (reference-code/jolt/stdlib/clojure/core/rrb_vector.clj), so a binary can require only what it compiled in, while bin/test (the runtime with deps resolved) loads it. It blocks `seon.source/the-tests-are-part-of-the-program`: `seon.print-test` requires `fipp.engine` (the layout's test oracle), so a root with `:seon.config.source/dirs [\"src\" \"test\"]` fails at boot, and an agent's fork could not run that test either. Correct: a built binary resolves a library it did not compile the way the runtime does (its stdlib embedded or found by absolute path, its deps' roots recorded at build), or the binary's build compiles what test/ requires; which one is a Jolt build decision for root (a dependency change waits for root's go). Then rerun the boot with run1.edn's dirs. Done by lane J1 (2026-10-21) the way Jolt's design already assumed (docs/forks.md, jolt section, `jolt/embed-stdlib`): `jolt build` gives an app that keeps the compiler jolt's install sources as one blob constant in its runtime unit (build.ss `bld-emit-install-sources`, io.ss `jolt-source-blob-attach-bytes!`); absolute roots were not taken, because Jolt's loader probes embedded keys first and #1232 made a binary independent of the build machine's paths. Measured on target/seon: binary 205.61 -> 206.51 MB, `seon ports` 0.63 -> 0.61 s, max RSS +1.9 MB, a root's boot with src 2.86 -> 2.78 s and with src and test 3.7 s (before: refused), `(require 'clojure.core.rrb-vector)` 6 ms and `fipp.engine` 30 ms from any cwd. Open: such a namespace compiles from source in every process (install-owned and embedded files are not AOT-cached); a cost only if a large one is reached."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.root-test/a-root-binary-requires-a-library-it-did-not-compile}}]
